REQP-1839#1 Warning
RAMB36 async control check
The RAMB36E1 u_safety_riscv_soc/core_b/u_ram/u_ram/mem_reg_0 has an input control pin u_safety_riscv_soc/core_b/u_ram/u_ram/mem_reg_0/ADDRARDADDR[14] (net: u_safety_riscv_soc/core_b/u_ram/u_ram/D[11]) which is driven by a register (u_safety_riscv_soc/core_b/u_ibex/gen_regfile_ff.register_file_i/g_plain_rf.g_rf_flops[10].rf_reg_q_reg[0]) that has an active asychronous set or reset. This may cause corruption of the memory contents and/or read values when the set/reset is asserted and is not analyzed by the default static timing analysis. It is suggested to eliminate the use of a set/reset to registers driving this RAMB pin or else use a synchronous reset in which the assertion of the reset is timed by default.
